{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>All these joined.</b> From the kal conjugation." "<b>The Siddim.</b> Like וְשִׁדְתָּם אֹתָם בַּשִּׁיד (Deuteronomy 27:2 et seq.) and וַתָּשֶׁם בַּסַּד רַגְלִי (Job 13:27), like פַת פְּתִים (i.e., a plural with duplicated final letters)." "<b>Valley.</b> It draws itself and another along with it, like אַל בְּאַפְּךָ תוֹכִיחֵנִי (Psalms 6:2), and so it is עֵמֶק יָם הַמֶּלַח."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:36.028068153Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}